def research_paragraph(title,subject,question,heading,marker,variant):
 if variant==1:
  return f'{title} asks {question}. During {heading.lower()}, the eligible population is a declared set of synthetic {subject} events from one decision window, and the observation unit is one event linked to source, actor, timestamp, owner, exception, and destination receipt. {marker}-A freezes inclusion and exclusion rules before outcomes are inspected. Reviewers label evidence confirmed, inferred, conflicting, unavailable, or awaiting decision; a ticket closure, automated acknowledgment, dashboard state, or matching count cannot substitute for the underlying event. The protocol is descriptive and does not rank providers, certify compliance, or predict performance outside the reviewed population.'
 return f'For {subject}, {marker}-B samples consecutive ordinary records plus boundary, failed, changed, reopened, and externally blocked cases. Preserve missing records in the denominator and use synthetic identifiers where a live record would expose candidate, worker, client, financial, credential, or communication data. Report observed count, exclusions, missingness, unresolved cases, median elapsed time, and tail cases by the declared cohort. A second reviewer independently applies the frozen codebook, records disagreement, and reconciles only after both readings are retained. Alternative explanations - including source latency, time-zone conversion, system batching, classification drift, and owner unavailability - must be tested before a causal claim. Public sources inform their own domains but do not establish a private provider outcome. Authorized buyer and provider owners retain commercial, employment, legal, privacy, security, access, and release decisions. Reproduce the selection rule, source versions, calculations, reviewer notes, exception dispositions, limitations, and owner acceptance before applying the finding to another period.'

